body:
As 4b04cb067c43edffc2e838358b5a597cf36cd283 in #249 `Enable -P if the compile will definitely be local`

```rust
    // When performing distributed compilation, line number info is important for error
    // reporting and to not cause spurious compilation failure (e.g. no exceptions build
    // fails due to exceptions transitively included in the stdlib).
    // With -fprofile-generate line number information is important, so don't use -P.
    if !may_dist && !parsed_args.profile_generate {
        cmd.arg("-P");
    }
```

but `-P` do conflict with `-g` ,   we need accurate line information while debug program, 

for example ,  test.cpp has two version

version 1:

```cpp
//line1
//line2
int i = 100;
```

version 2:

```cpp
//line1
int i = 100;
```

compile two version with `sccache g++  -g  -c test.cpp ` ,   there will hit with same key, 
while come to debug, line will be in a mess

That will be appreciated if sccache support bypass `-P` on configuarion or `-g`

BR.
